 "series_identification": "Confirmed from legends: black = Limit Analysis upper bound solution (Gamma), red = Limit Equilibrium - Cho [19] (F_s). Fig 21/22 left = F_s (red), right = Gamma (black). All axes are linear; quantities are dimensionless (PDF in 1/unit, CDF probability).",
 "findings": [
  "Axis calibration confirmed. Raster-detected tick positions agree with the extractor's to <= 0.04 pt on every axis, and tick values (Fig17 x 0.5-2.0, y 0-2 / 0-1; Fig21 x 0-3 / 0-6, y 0-3 / 0-0.8; Fig22 x 0-2 / 0-8, y 0-1) were confirmed visually. The axes are linear, not log.",
  "53 point checks across all 8 series. Every one is within 2% relative: the max is 1.65%, at a small density value (Fig17 black PDF, x=0.9), and the max difference is 0.37% of axis span. Median raster-to-polyline distance is <= 0.05 pt for every series (the stroke width is 0.71-1.05 pt).",
  "One apparent outlier, Fig17 black PDF at x=1.40, came from my first occlusion heuristic. Inspecting the raster column showed a separate black run centred at 1.500, which confirms the extractor value of 1.4998.",
  "The statistics recomputed from the extractor's points reproduce theirs to <= 1e-4 (mean, std, median, P(<1), raw area, and CDF-derived mean/std).",
  "Mode differences: the extractor reports a parabola-fit mode, while the linear argmax gives 1.231/1.230/1.156/1.394 against their 1.229/1.226/1.164/1.427. The largest gap (Fig21 Gamma, 2.3%) is inside the stated +-0.05 uncertainty, and the JSON also stores mode_argmax=1.3937.",
  "Raster CDF readings agree with the extractor: medians to <= 0.0004, and P(<1) of 6.44/7.60/5.25/5.53% against 6.46/7.61/5.15/5.52%. The largest relative gap is 1.9%, for Cho F_s in Ex 5.3.2 (0.1 pp absolute, about 1 px).",
  "Confirmed that the Cho F_s red PDF in Fig 21 is inconsistent with the red CDF in Fig 22: the integrated raster PDF exceeds the plotted CDF by up to about 0.03. Also confirmed that the KDE PDF of Gamma (5.3.2) gives P(<1) of about 6.6%, against 5.5% from the CDF.",
  "Confirmed that the curves are outlined filled polygons and that the hidden parts beyond the clip exist in the vector data (e.g. Fig17 black PDF fill bbox to x=2.775; Fig21 Gamma to 6.48). These parts cannot be checked by the raster method because they are invisible, but their bounding boxes match.",
  "Paper text values were rechecked: Pf = 6.5% (LA) and 7.9% (Cho) for 5.3.1, and 5.50% (LA) and 6.37% (Cho) for 5.3.2. They are correctly quoted."
 ],
